# The five testdata variants are GENERATED by ./sync-testdata.sh from testdata/app/
# plus the real skill at ../../skills/security/.
#
# They are not committed on purpose: each embeds a full copy of the skill (~85 KB x 5),
# and a committed copy would silently drift from the skill it is supposed to be testing —
# the bench would then measure a stale snapshot while reporting on the current skill.
#
# Run ./sync-testdata.sh before ./madbench *.yaml. The generator verifies each variant
# differs from `bare` by exactly the one intended file and fails loudly otherwise.
testdata/bare/
testdata/routed/
testdata/listed/
testdata/canary/
testdata/readrow/

# Sandbox leftovers if a bench is ever run in-place.
node_modules/
bun.lock
*.report.json
